        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;My sister is fading. The house is cold. And outside… things are getting worse.&quot;</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It's 1934. The world is fragile. People are quiet, hungry, scared. But still, every day, someone knocks on the door. And someone must choose who to let in.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as a man caring for his sick sister in a decaying home. Each day brings a visitor — a beggar, a liar, a prophet, a stranger. Your answers shape their fate, and yours. Help costs resources. Refusal may cost your soul.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every decision is recorded in a diary. And the diary remembers more than you do.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Key Features:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >– Every choice changes the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >– Atmospheric story-driven game set in 1934<br>– Simple but weighty choices with lasting impact<br>– Morality, supplies, and conscience define your survival<br>– Stylized 2D visuals, minimal controls<br>– Slow-paced, emotionally heavy experience with branching dialogue</p>",
